1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,920
Bid Intake brings incoming bid emails into one
review queue.

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:05,705
This walkthrough uses training examples.

3
00:00:05,705 --> 00:00:09,632
Start with Needs review, switch to Due soon for
approaching deadlines,

4
00:00:09,632 --> 00:00:11,417
or search for a venue.

5
00:00:11,417 --> 00:00:15,344
Select a bid to keep its next action beside the
evidence.

6
00:00:16,444 --> 00:00:21,281
Summary and dates shows the request, the deadline,
and the exact words supporting it.

7
00:00:21,281 --> 00:00:23,699
Check that evidence before changing a deal.

8
00:00:23,699 --> 00:00:26,463
Open Original email to read the full message,

9
00:00:26,463 --> 00:00:30,263
then return to the summary when you are ready to
decide.

10
00:00:31,363 --> 00:00:34,476
Choose the matching opportunity and review the
confirmation.

11
00:00:34,476 --> 00:00:36,422
The current deadline stays visible.

12
00:00:36,422 --> 00:00:42,259
Clear the deadline checkbox when you want to keep
the dates already in the CRM.

13
00:00:42,259 --> 00:00:44,594
Confirm and apply saves the decision.

14
00:00:44,594 --> 00:00:46,540
Cancel returns you to review.

15
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:51,512
For a message you need to add yourself, open Process
an email.

16
00:00:51,512 --> 00:00:56,029
Enter the subject and sender, then paste the full
message, including the deadline wording.

17
00:00:56,029 --> 00:00:59,578
Extract and match prepares it for review in the same
queue.

18
00:01:00,678 --> 00:01:03,749
Bid Alerts explains what happened after an email was
checked.

19
00:01:03,749 --> 00:01:08,048
Filter by outcome, open an entry, and read why it
was held or announced.

20
00:01:08,048 --> 00:01:09,276
Tests stay clearly labeled.

21
00:01:09,276 --> 00:01:12,347
Review source email takes you back to the original
bid,

22
00:01:12,347 --> 00:01:15,725
so you can check the evidence and choose the next
action.
